W-4: set the cmdline cvar on the shareware arm of COM_CheckRegistered.

The stall that ate three Pi runs was never graphics: johnfitz rewrote
Cmd_StuffCmds_f to read the "cmdline" CVAR (for dynamic mod loading),
and COM_CheckRegistered sets that cvar ONLY on the registered arm --
the shareware arm returns first. With shareware pak0.pak every
+command on the command line is silently discarded: +timedemo demo1
never entered the cbuf, startdemos took the QuakeSpasm no-fitzmode
path (straight to menu_main, no demo loop), and the game sat at the
main menu rendering at a healthy ~17 fps -- ~35 venus fences/s, all
retiring, zero parks (the warp-watch ledger named it) -- while the
harness waited for an fps line that could never come.

tyrquake's Cmd_StuffCmds_f still parses com_argv directly and is
immune, which is why the GL leg's +timedemo works on the same pak.
This patch mirrors the registered arm's leading-space skip +
Cvar_SetROM onto the shareware arm, restoring original-Quake
+command semantics for shareware content.

--- a/Quake/common.c	2026-08-31 20:04:04
+++ b/Quake/common.c	2026-08-31 20:04:12
@@ -1290,6 +1290,19 @@
 
 	if (h == -1)
 	{
+		/* THYLACINE port (0004): set the cmdline cvar on THIS arm too.
+		 * johnfitz's Cmd_StuffCmds_f reads the "cmdline" CVAR (not
+		 * com_argv, which tyrquake still parses and is immune), and
+		 * only the registered arm below ever set it -- so on shareware
+		 * content every +command was silently discarded: +timedemo
+		 * never entered the cbuf and the QuakeSpasm no-fitzmode
+		 * startdemos path parked the game at menu_main forever. */
+		for (i = 0; com_cmdline[i]; i++)
+		{
+			if (com_cmdline[i]!= ' ')
+				break;
+		}
+		Cvar_SetROM ("cmdline", &com_cmdline[i]);
 		Cvar_SetROM ("registered", "0");
 		Con_Printf ("Playing shareware version.\n");
 		if (com_modified)
